{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj8y44B8zcJsKGpw7jFw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016caEJ2kMdKGvqS6kt3NAg4","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work/_research/engine/unpacked/pixel-engine/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2522,"cache_read_input_tokens":25523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2522},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b0c7f2-b636-4810-bb2b-a989930a5e0b","uuid":"e10e68e7-fd65-4770-aebd-edb2fb6a0be4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:19:21.916Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj8y3bthFnqyujXy4HRV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016caEJ2kMdKGvqS6kt3NAg4":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work/_research/engine/unpacked/pixel-engine/README.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016caEJ2kMdKGvqS6kt3NAg4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Pixel Engine 0.46.0\n2\t\n3\tA WebGPU engine that renders 3D scenes as authentic pixel art (WebGPU only), with\n4\tRapier physics, a platformer character with a full animation set, pixel HUD, audio, particles\n5\tand a look system (filters per layer). This folder is everything a game needs.\n6\t\n7\tRead in this order:\n8\t\n9\t1. `GUIDE.md` (~15k tokens): how to host a game, the mental model, a complete game, recipes, the rules and common mistakes. Read it whole.\n10\t2. `API.md` (~62k tokens): every export with its signature and doc. Search it; don't read it whole.\n11\t3. `game.js`: the guide's quick start, a complete game. Edit it into yours.\n12\t4. `ASSETS.md` (~4k tokens), when the game builds with models and textures: the library, the format, the loop and the style rules. Read it whole; `LIBRARY.md` (~44k tokens) lists every model and texture, built in or from a pack: search it (or filter `library.json`).\n13\t\n14\t| File | What |\n15\t| --- | --- |\n16\t| `pixel-engine.js` | The engine, 4750 KB: one ES module with three.js (`THREE`, `TSL`), Rapier and its wasm, the hero kit, the built-in models (`assets/coin.glb`, `assets/hero.glb`, `assets/tree.glb`) and the engine CSS. Never edit it. |\n17\t| `index.html`, `game.js` | A game to start from: serve this folder over HTTP and open `index.html` |\n18\t| `examples/` | The guides' other recipes as pages (`side-scroller`, `top-down`, `looks`, `market`) and the modules they import (`market-models.js`) |\n19\t| `check.mjs` | `node check.mjs [page] [--keys KeyD*60,Space*4] [--cameras] [--looks a,b]`: plays the page in a real browser, saves screenshots, fails on any error. Run it before you hand a game back. `node check.mjs --headless game.js` plays the game in Node with no browser and replays it (GUIDE.md section 8); `node check.mjs --sheets models.js` draws your models and textures (ASSETS.md) |\n20\t| `ASSETS.md`, `LIBRARY.md`, `CREDITS.md` | Models and textures as data; the built-in library and the imported packs, by family; where everything the kit carries came from (ship it with your game) |\n21\t| `library.json` | Every model and texture as data (id, kind, family, pack, tags, size, licence): filter it to find what a game needs |\n22\t| `packs/` | Imported packs (`packs/index.json` lists them): `loadPack('packs/<id>.json')` |\n23\t| `pixel-engine.d.ts`, `types/` | TypeScript declarations (optional) |\n24\t| `CHANGELOG.md` | What changed between engine versions |\n25\t| `LICENSE` | The engine's licence (MIT) |\n26\t| `manifest.json` | Version, build, where newer versions are (`latest`, `releases`, `source`) and every file with its size |\n27\t\n28\tServe it: `npx serve .` or `python3 -m http.server` here, then open http://localhost:3000/ (or :8000).\n29\tES modules don't load from `file://`.\n30\t\n31\tNewer versions: the newest release of the kit is always https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, and every release stays\n32\tat https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases with what changed in it. To build one from\n33\tthe engine's repository instead: `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight && cd riftlight && npm ci && npm run bundle`\n34\tmakes `bundle/pixel-engine/`. To upgrade a game, see GUIDE.md, section 10.\n35\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b0c7f2-b636-4810-bb2b-a989930a5e0b","uuid":"de4a1264-2853-4d8b-be9c-5e1e409764bc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:19:21.923Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work/_research/engine/unpacked/pixel-engine/README.md","content":"# Pixel Engine 0.46.0\n\nA WebGPU engine that renders 3D scenes as authentic pixel art (WebGPU only), with\nRapier physics, a platformer character with a full animation set, pixel HUD, audio, particles\nand a look system (filters per layer). This folder is everything a game needs.\n\nRead in this order:\n\n1. `GUIDE.md` (~15k tokens): how to host a game, the mental model, a complete game, recipes, the rules and common mistakes. Read it whole.\n2. `API.md` (~62k tokens): every export with its signature and doc. Search it; don't read it whole.\n3. `game.js`: the guide's quick start, a complete game. Edit it into yours.\n4. `ASSETS.md` (~4k tokens), when the game builds with models and textures: the library, the format, the loop and the style rules. Read it whole; `LIBRARY.md` (~44k tokens) lists every model and texture, built in or from a pack: search it (or filter `library.json`).\n\n| File | What |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pixel-engine.js` | The engine, 4750 KB: one ES module with three.js (`THREE`, `TSL`), Rapier and its wasm, the hero kit, the built-in models (`assets/coin.glb`, `assets/hero.glb`, `assets/tree.glb`) and the engine CSS. Never edit it. |\n| `index.html`, `game.js` | A game to start from: serve this folder over HTTP and open `index.html` |\n| `examples/` | The guides' other recipes as pages (`side-scroller`, `top-down`, `looks`, `market`) and the modules they import (`market-models.js`) |\n| `check.mjs` | `node check.mjs [page] [--keys KeyD*60,Space*4] [--cameras] [--looks a,b]`: plays the page in a real browser, saves screenshots, fails on any error. Run it before you hand a game back. `node check.mjs --headless game.js` plays the game in Node with no browser and replays it (GUIDE.md section 8); `node check.mjs --sheets models.js` draws your models and textures (ASSETS.md) |\n| `ASSETS.md`, `LIBRARY.md`, `CREDITS.md` | Models and textures as data; the built-in library and the imported packs, by family; where everything the kit carries came from (ship it with your game) |\n| `library.json` | Every model and texture as data (id, kind, family, pack, tags, size, licence): filter it to find what a game needs |\n| `packs/` | Imported packs (`packs/index.json` lists them): `loadPack('packs/<id>.json')` |\n| `pixel-engine.d.ts`, `types/` | TypeScript declarations (optional) |\n| `CHANGELOG.md` | What changed between engine versions |\n| `LICENSE` | The engine's licence (MIT) |\n| `manifest.json` | Version, build, where newer versions are (`latest`, `releases`, `source`) and every file with its size |\n\nServe it: `npx serve .` or `python3 -m http.server` here, then open http://localhost:3000/ (or :8000).\nES modules don't load from `file://`.\n\nNewer versions: the newest release of the kit is always https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, and every release stays\nat https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases with what changed in it. To build one from\nthe engine's repository instead: `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight && cd riftlight && npm ci && npm run bundle`\nmakes `bundle/pixel-engine/`. To upgrade a game, see GUIDE.md, section 10.\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016caEJ2kMdKGvqS6kt3NAg4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
