{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj95xhQsKzwmoQevXfDx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y251XzN8SEeachhDCdxsNY","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work/_research/engine/unpacked/pixel-engine/API.md","offset":2132,"limit":108},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21319,"cache_read_input_tokens":113804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21319},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b0c7f2-b636-4810-bb2b-a989930a5e0b","uuid":"93e7bc94-31aa-4a07-9778-b6e2e8f6ead1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:58.362Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj95xTXgJUzwM7ZnyJks","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Y251XzN8SEeachhDCdxsNY":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work/_research/engine/unpacked/pixel-engine/API.md","offset":2132,"limit":108}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y251XzN8SEeachhDCdxsNY","type":"tool_result","content":"2132\t## 6. Characters\n2133\t\n2134\t### type JumpKind\n2135\t\n2136\t```ts\n2137\ttype JumpKind = 'Jump' | 'JumpUp' | 'DoubleJump' | 'TripleJump' | 'Backflip' | 'SideFlip' | 'LongJump' | 'WallKick' | 'JumpKick'\n2138\t```\n2139\t\n2140\t### KEYMAP\n2141\t\n2142\t```ts\n2143\tconst KEYMAP: { readonly jump: readonly [\"Space\"]; readonly walk: readonly [\"ShiftLeft\", \"ShiftRight\"]; readonly crouch: readonly [\"KeyC\", \"ControlLeft\", \"ControlRight\"]; readonly prone: readonly [\"KeyZ\"]; readonly lie: readonly [\"KeyX\"]; readonly grab: readonly [...]; readonly attack: readonly [...]; readonly wave: readonly [......\n2144\t```\n2145\t\n2146\tDefault key map for PlatformerCharacter. Movement is camera-relative for every preset\n2147\t(strafing in first person; left/right only on a side-scroller lane, except while\n2148\tclimbing or hanging). Call from Game.fixedUpdate.\n2149\t\n2150\t  WASD / arrows  move          Shift   walk / tiptoe\n2151\t  Space          jump          C / Ctrl crouch (air: ground pound)\n2152\t  Z              prone toggle  X        lie down / get up\n2153\t  F (hold)       grab / pull   J        attack (punch, punch, kick; air: dive / kick)\n2154\t  V              wave          B        sit\n2155\t\n2156\t### interface MoveInput\n2157\t\n2158\t- `move: Vector3`: Desired horizontal direction in world space, length 0..1.\n2159\t- `walk?: boolean`: Walk / tiptoe modifier.\n2160\t- `jump: boolean`\n2161\t- `jumpHeld: boolean`\n2162\t- `crouch: boolean`: Crouch (held).\n2163\t- `crouchPressed?: boolean`: Crouch pressed this step (in the air: ground pound).\n2164\t- `prone?: boolean`: Toggle prone (pressed).\n2165\t- `lie?: boolean`: Toggle lying on the back (pressed).\n2166\t- `grab?: boolean`: Grab / pull (held).\n2167\t- `attack?: boolean`\n2168\t- `wave?: boolean`\n2169\t- `sit?: boolean`\n2170\t- `face?: Vector3 | null`: First person: always face this direction and strafe.\n2171\t\n2172\t### type MoveState\n2173\t\n2174\t```ts\n2175\ttype MoveState = keyof typeof STATES\n2176\t```\n2177\t\n2178\t### class PlatformerCharacter\n2179\t\n2180\t- `new PlatformerCharacter(physics: Physics, options: PlatformerOptions)`\n2181\t- `readonly body: RAPIER.RigidBody`\n2182\t- `readonly collider: RAPIER.Collider`\n2183\t- `readonly kcc: RAPIER.KinematicCharacterController`\n2184\t- `state: MoveState`\n2185\t- `stateTime: number`\n2186\t- `jumpKind: JumpKind`\n2187\t- `facing: number`: Yaw in radians (0 = facing +Z).\n2188\t- `readonly hvel: Vector3`: Horizontal velocity (world).\n2189\t- `vy: number`\n2190\t- `grounded: boolean`\n2191\t- `stance: Stance`\n2192\t- `anim: string`: Last animation clip requested (for tests / debug UI).\n2193\t- `readonly stats: { jumps: number; landings: number; ledgeGrabs: number; pullUps: number; pushes: number; pulls: number; hurts: number; crushes: number; }`: Counters for tests/tooling.\n2194\t- `groundCollider: number`: The collider under the feet (its handle; -1 in the air). A moving platform's, a conveyor's or a dynamic plank's: the character rides it (`move`).\n2195\t- `weight: number`: How hard the character presses the dynamic floor it stands on (a rope bridge sags where it stands, a spring pad sinks), in the physics world's mass units (density × m³: a 1 m crate of density 2 weighs 2), under the world's gravity. 0 (the default): it rides d…\n2196\t- `shove: number`: The most mass the character shoves at walking speed when it walks into a loose dynamic body (a swing door, a ball, a hanging bag, debris); heavier bodies move proportionally less. 0 (the default): dynamic bodies block like walls. Bodies tagged `pushable` are…\n2197\t- `crushed: boolean`: A moving body is coming down on the head with the floor underneath: squeezed (a lift lowering onto the character, a crusher). `stats.crushes` counts each one; games decide what it does (hurt, respawn): the character itself just stays on the floor.\n2198\t- `invulnerable: number`: Seconds left in which hits are ignored (after `hurt`). Games can blink the model meanwhile.\n2199\t- `lookAt: Vector3 | null`: Something worth looking at (world position), set by the game: a coin, an enemy, a sign. Standing and walking, the head turns toward it (within its limits); null = look where the character is going.\n2200\t- `climb: number`: Smoothed grade of the ground being covered (rise per metre; + = uphill).\n2201\t- `get feet: Vector3`: Feet position (bottom of the capsule). Allocates: hot paths use `feetInto`.\n2202\t- `feetInto(target: Vector3): Vector3`: `feet` without allocating: writes the feet position into `target`.\n2203\t- `interpolatedFeet(alpha: number, target = new Vector3()): Vector3`: Feet between the last two fixed steps (render interpolation), into `target`.\n2204\t- `get forward: Vector3`: Facing direction (horizontal, unit). Allocates: hot paths use `forwardInto`.\n2205\t- `forwardInto(target: Vector3): Vector3`: `forward` without allocating.\n2206\t- `get speed: number`\n2207\t- `eye(alpha = 1): Vector3`: Eye position for first-person cameras.\n2208\t- `setLockDepth(on: boolean): void`: Side-scroller lane lock on/off (locks to the current Z).\n2209\t- `teleport(position: [number, number, number]): void`\n2210\t- `jump(kind: JumpKind, input?: MoveInput): void`: Jump right now (no headroom: nothing happens). Normally the state machine decides.\n2211\t- `hurt(fromDirection: Vector3, strength = 1): boolean`: Get hit: knocked back away from `fromDirection` (where the hit came from, e.g. enemy position minus hero position; only its horizontal part counts) in an arc, playing Hurt, with no control for ~0.4 s, then invulnerable for a moment (`invulnerable`). `strength…\n2212\t- `launch(vy: number, o: { hvel?: Vector3; kind?: JumpKind } = {}): void`: Thrown into the air at `vy` m/s (a trampoline, a spring, a geyser): a jump whose arc no button can cut short. `hvel` replaces the horizontal velocity (default: kept).\n2213\t- `celebrate(): void`: Celebrate (games call this, e.g. on level complete).\n2214\t- `fixedUpdate(dt: number, input: MoveInput): void`\n2215\t- `findLedge(feet: Vector3, dir: Vector3): Ledge | null`: Find a grabbable ledge in front of `feet` (facing `dir`).\n2216\t- `uphillSpeed(): number`: Top running speed on this ground: Mario 64 slows going uphill (the steeper, the slower; too steep to stand on slides back, see checkSlope). Stairs count by their average climb.\n2217\t- `setStance(stance: Stance, force = false): boolean`: Change collider height, keeping the feet planted. Growing needs headroom unless forced.\n2218\t- `attachModel(model: Object3D, clips: readonly AnimationClip[], rig?: RigSpec): void`: Drive `model` with `clips`. Call again (e.g. on hot reload) to swap the clip set. With the model's `rig`, the procedural layers run too: foot placement on the real ground, leaning into turns, looking ahead, landing squash (docs/ANIMATION.md).\n2219\t- `animationMix(): { name: string; weight: number; time: number; rate: number }[]`: Tooling: every clip currently contributing to the pose, with its blend weight and time (s).\n2220\t- `footPlacement(): FootPlacementState | null`: Tooling: what foot placement did this frame (weight, pelvis drop, per-foot offsets and locks).\n2221\t- `clipDuration(name: string, fallback: number): number`\n2222\t- `animationFor(): AnimRequest`: Name of the clip the current state wants (the table's `anim`).\n2223\t- `updateVisual(model: Object3D, dt: number, alpha: number): void`: Per render frame: orient the model, pick and advance animation, then the procedural layers.\n2224\t\n2225\t### interface PlatformerOptions\n2226\t\n2227\t- `position: [number, number, number]`\n2228\t- `lockDepth?: boolean`: Side-scroller: keep the character on its starting Z lane.\n2229\t- `runSpeed?: number`\n2230\t\n2231\t### readMoveInput()\n2232\t\n2233\t```ts\n2234\tfunction readMoveInput(ctx: GameContext, character: PlatformerCharacter, out?: MoveInput): MoveInput\n2235\t```\n2236\t\n2237\tRead the default key map into a MoveInput. Pass `out` (kept by the game) to reuse it and\n2238\tits `move` vector every step instead of allocating a new one.\n2239\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b0c7f2-b636-4810-bb2b-a989930a5e0b","uuid":"ba5b14d5-d543-4f6e-a58c-c4b3f3559d46","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:20:58.369Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work/_research/engine/unpacked/pixel-engine/API.md","content":"## 6. Characters\n\n### type JumpKind\n\n```ts\ntype JumpKind = 'Jump' | 'JumpUp' | 'DoubleJump' | 'TripleJump' | 'Backflip' | 'SideFlip' | 'LongJump' | 'WallKick' | 'JumpKick'\n```\n\n### KEYMAP\n\n```ts\nconst KEYMAP: { readonly jump: readonly [\"Space\"]; readonly walk: readonly [\"ShiftLeft\", \"ShiftRight\"]; readonly crouch: readonly [\"KeyC\", \"ControlLeft\", \"ControlRight\"]; readonly prone: readonly [\"KeyZ\"]; readonly lie: readonly [\"KeyX\"]; readonly grab: readonly [...]; readonly attack: readonly [...]; readonly wave: readonly [......\n```\n\nDefault key map for PlatformerCharacter. Movement is camera-relative for every preset\n(strafing in first person; left/right only on a side-scroller lane, except while\nclimbing or hanging). Call from Game.fixedUpdate.\n\n  WASD / arrows  move          Shift   walk / tiptoe\n  Space          jump          C / Ctrl crouch (air: ground pound)\n  Z              prone toggle  X        lie down / get up\n  F (hold)       grab / pull   J        attack (punch, punch, kick; air: dive / kick)\n  V              wave          B        sit\n\n### interface MoveInput\n\n- `move: Vector3`: Desired horizontal direction in world space, length 0..1.\n- `walk?: boolean`: Walk / tiptoe modifier.\n- `jump: boolean`\n- `jumpHeld: boolean`\n- `crouch: boolean`: Crouch (held).\n- `crouchPressed?: boolean`: Crouch pressed this step (in the air: ground pound).\n- `prone?: boolean`: Toggle prone (pressed).\n- `lie?: boolean`: Toggle lying on the back (pressed).\n- `grab?: boolean`: Grab / pull (held).\n- `attack?: boolean`\n- `wave?: boolean`\n- `sit?: boolean`\n- `face?: Vector3 | null`: First person: always face this direction and strafe.\n\n### type MoveState\n\n```ts\ntype MoveState = keyof typeof STATES\n```\n\n### class PlatformerCharacter\n\n- `new PlatformerCharacter(physics: Physics, options: PlatformerOptions)`\n- `readonly body: RAPIER.RigidBody`\n- `readonly collider: RAPIER.Collider`\n- `readonly kcc: RAPIER.KinematicCharacterController`\n- `state: MoveState`\n- `stateTime: number`\n- `jumpKind: JumpKind`\n- `facing: number`: Yaw in radians (0 = facing +Z).\n- `readonly hvel: Vector3`: Horizontal velocity (world).\n- `vy: number`\n- `grounded: boolean`\n- `stance: Stance`\n- `anim: string`: Last animation clip requested (for tests / debug UI).\n- `readonly stats: { jumps: number; landings: number; ledgeGrabs: number; pullUps: number; pushes: number; pulls: number; hurts: number; crushes: number; }`: Counters for tests/tooling.\n- `groundCollider: number`: The collider under the feet (its handle; -1 in the air). A moving platform's, a conveyor's or a dynamic plank's: the character rides it (`move`).\n- `weight: number`: How hard the character presses the dynamic floor it stands on (a rope bridge sags where it stands, a spring pad sinks), in the physics world's mass units (density × m³: a 1 m crate of density 2 weighs 2), under the world's gravity. 0 (the default): it rides d…\n- `shove: number`: The most mass the character shoves at walking speed when it walks into a loose dynamic body (a swing door, a ball, a hanging bag, debris); heavier bodies move proportionally less. 0 (the default): dynamic bodies block like walls. Bodies tagged `pushable` are…\n- `crushed: boolean`: A moving body is coming down on the head with the floor underneath: squeezed (a lift lowering onto the character, a crusher). `stats.crushes` counts each one; games decide what it does (hurt, respawn): the character itself just stays on the floor.\n- `invulnerable: number`: Seconds left in which hits are ignored (after `hurt`). Games can blink the model meanwhile.\n- `lookAt: Vector3 | null`: Something worth looking at (world position), set by the game: a coin, an enemy, a sign. Standing and walking, the head turns toward it (within its limits); null = look where the character is going.\n- `climb: number`: Smoothed grade of the ground being covered (rise per metre; + = uphill).\n- `get feet: Vector3`: Feet position (bottom of the capsule). Allocates: hot paths use `feetInto`.\n- `feetInto(target: Vector3): Vector3`: `feet` without allocating: writes the feet position into `target`.\n- `interpolatedFeet(alpha: number, target = new Vector3()): Vector3`: Feet between the last two fixed steps (render interpolation), into `target`.\n- `get forward: Vector3`: Facing direction (horizontal, unit). Allocates: hot paths use `forwardInto`.\n- `forwardInto(target: Vector3): Vector3`: `forward` without allocating.\n- `get speed: number`\n- `eye(alpha = 1): Vector3`: Eye position for first-person cameras.\n- `setLockDepth(on: boolean): void`: Side-scroller lane lock on/off (locks to the current Z).\n- `teleport(position: [number, number, number]): void`\n- `jump(kind: JumpKind, input?: MoveInput): void`: Jump right now (no headroom: nothing happens). Normally the state machine decides.\n- `hurt(fromDirection: Vector3, strength = 1): boolean`: Get hit: knocked back away from `fromDirection` (where the hit came from, e.g. enemy position minus hero position; only its horizontal part counts) in an arc, playing Hurt, with no control for ~0.4 s, then invulnerable for a moment (`invulnerable`). `strength…\n- `launch(vy: number, o: { hvel?: Vector3; kind?: JumpKind } = {}): void`: Thrown into the air at `vy` m/s (a trampoline, a spring, a geyser): a jump whose arc no button can cut short. `hvel` replaces the horizontal velocity (default: kept).\n- `celebrate(): void`: Celebrate (games call this, e.g. on level complete).\n- `fixedUpdate(dt: number, input: MoveInput): void`\n- `findLedge(feet: Vector3, dir: Vector3): Ledge | null`: Find a grabbable ledge in front of `feet` (facing `dir`).\n- `uphillSpeed(): number`: Top running speed on this ground: Mario 64 slows going uphill (the steeper, the slower; too steep to stand on slides back, see checkSlope). Stairs count by their average climb.\n- `setStance(stance: Stance, force = false): boolean`: Change collider height, keeping the feet planted. Growing needs headroom unless forced.\n- `attachModel(model: Object3D, clips: readonly AnimationClip[], rig?: RigSpec): void`: Drive `model` with `clips`. Call again (e.g. on hot reload) to swap the clip set. With the model's `rig`, the procedural layers run too: foot placement on the real ground, leaning into turns, looking ahead, landing squash (docs/ANIMATION.md).\n- `animationMix(): { name: string; weight: number; time: number; rate: number }[]`: Tooling: every clip currently contributing to the pose, with its blend weight and time (s).\n- `footPlacement(): FootPlacementState | null`: Tooling: what foot placement did this frame (weight, pelvis drop, per-foot offsets and locks).\n- `clipDuration(name: string, fallback: number): number`\n- `animationFor(): AnimRequest`: Name of the clip the current state wants (the table's `anim`).\n- `updateVisual(model: Object3D, dt: number, alpha: number): void`: Per render frame: orient the model, pick and advance animation, then the procedural layers.\n\n### interface PlatformerOptions\n\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\n- `lockDepth?: boolean`: Side-scroller: keep the character on its starting Z lane.\n- `runSpeed?: number`\n\n### readMoveInput()\n\n```ts\nfunction readMoveInput(ctx: GameContext, character: PlatformerCharacter, out?: MoveInput): MoveInput\n```\n\nRead the default key map into a MoveInput. Pass `out` (kept by the game) to reuse it and\nits `move` vector every step instead of allocating a new one.\n","numLines":108,"startLine":2132,"totalLines":5144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Y251XzN8SEeachhDCdxsNY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
