dth\": 720, \"cssHeight\": 540, \"offsetX\": 40, \"offsetY\": 30}, \"hud\": [360, 270], \"ptr\": {\"x\": -0.5555555555555556, \"y\": -0.5555555555555556, \"over\": true, \"touch\": false}, \"over\": true, \"canvas\": [40, 30, 720, 540], \"hudRect\": [40, 30, 720, 540], \"hudBack\": [360, 270]}\npad {\"connected\": true, \"padAxis\": {\"x\": 0, \"y\": 0}, \"move\": {\"x\": 0, \"y\": 0}, \"mouseDeltaFromRStick\": {\"x\": 0, \"y\": 0}, \"crossDown\": true, \"r2Down\": true, \"held\": [\"PadCross\", \"PadR2\"]}\ntouch {\"touchObj\": true, \"coarse\": true, \"hoverNone\": true, \"anyFine\": false, \"maxTouch\": 1, \"res\": {\"width\": 158, \"height\": 270}, \"hud\": [480, 270], \"dom\": \"DIV.pixel-loading B. DIV.bar I.on I.on I.on I.on I.on I.on I.on I.on I.on\"}\ndesktop {'coarse': False, 'hoverNone': False, 'anyFine': True, 'maxTouch': 0}\n4881:### class Timeline\n4882-\n4883-- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n4884-- `readonly duration: number`\n4885-- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n4886-- `playing: boolean`\n4887-- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n4888-- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n4889-- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n4890-- `play(): void`\n4891-- `pause(): void`\n4892-- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n4893-- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while \n4894-- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n4895-- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a \n4896-- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n4897-- `bars(t = this.time): number`: How far the letterbox bars are in (0..1) at `t` (default now): sliding in at the start, out at the end.\n4898-\n4899-### interface TimelineLine\n4900-\n4901-- `at: number`\n4902-- `until: number`\n4903-- `text: string`\n4904-- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n4905-\n4906-### interface TimelineOptions\n4907-\n### class CameraRig\n\nBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n\n- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n- `zoom: number`\n- `readonly minZoom: number`\n- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking thi\n- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\n- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n- `state(): CameraRigState`: The rig as data, exact (`engine.snapshot()`).\n- `setState(s: CameraRigState): void`: Put the rig back where `state()` found it (the same preset).\n\n### interface Framing\n\n- `readonly artWidth: number`: Art (internal) resolution actually rendered. Equals `internal` in fixed mode.\n- `readonly artHeight: number`\n- `readonly scale: number`: Device pixels per art pixel. Integer whenever `integer` is true.\n- `readonly integer: boolean`: True when every art pixel maps to an integer block of device pixels.\n- `readonly canvasWidth: number`: Canvas backing-store size in device pixels.\n- `readonly canvasHeight: number`\n- `readonly cssWidth: number`: Canvas CSS size and offset inside the viewport, in CSS pixels.\n- `readonly cssHeight: number`\n- `readonly offsetX: number`\n- `readonly offsetY: number`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01A1ispRLihQV8dP6wHEVbT7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
