{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wg25LxJwSiEVDLVNQmitCJ","type":"tool_result","content":"175-     * tools. Default: on with the debug panel (dev, ?debug=1), off in a shipped game, whose players\n176-     * have the same options in the settings. `true` / `false`: always on / off; an object rebinds\n177-     * or disables (null) single actions, and they still come with the debug panel.\n178-     */\n179-    debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption;\n180-    /**\n181-     * The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate,\n182-     * sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true:\n183-     * 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for none: open the\n184-     * panel from your own menu (`engine.settings.open()`). `key`: where they are saved\n185-     * (localStorage `pixel-engine:settings:<key>`; default the first game's name), false: nowhere.\n186-     */\n187:    settings?: {\n### QUALITY\n\n```ts\nconst QUALITY: Readonly<Record<QualityLevel, QualitySettings>>\n```\n\nAt the iso preset's default zoom the shadow box spans ~30 world units, i.e. ~600 art\npixels: 512² is about one shadow texel per art pixel, 1024² is finer than the art can show.\n\n### QUALITY_LEVELS\n\n```ts\nconst QUALITY_LEVELS: readonly QualityLevel[]\n```\n\n### QUALITY_OPTIONS\n\n```ts\nconst QUALITY_OPTIONS: readonly QualityOption[]\n```\n\n4469:### class Mirror\n4470-\n4471-- `new Mirror(o: MirrorOptions = {})`\n4472-- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n4473-- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n4474-- `enabled: boolean`: False: the glass shows plain glass and nothing is rendered for it.\n4475-- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n4476-- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene, camera: Camera, width: number, height: number): boolean`: Reflect `camera` in the glass and draw `scene` from there into the texture (sized `widt\n4477-- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`), from its camera, at its art size. Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never ru\n4478-- `dispose(): void`\n4479-\n4480-### interface MirrorOptions\n4481-\n4127:### class Decals\n4128-\n4129-- `new Decals(scene: Scene, o: { capacity?: number } = {})`\n4130-- `readonly meshes: Map<\"ring\" | \"crack\" | \"footprint\" | \"scorch\" | \"splat\", InstancedMesh<BufferGeometry<NormalBufferAttributes, BufferGeometryEventMap>, Material<...> | Material…`\n3911:### applySky()\n3912-\n3913-```ts\n3914-function applySky(engine: Pick<Engine, 'sun' | 'ambient' | 'scene' | 'setSunDirection'>, s: SkyState): void\n3915-```\n3916-\n--\n4733:### skyAt()\n4734-\n4735-```ts\n4736-function skyAt(hour: number): SkyState\n4737-```\n4738-\nOK  built.html  (WebGPU, engine 0.46.0, 36 frames, \"spike avatars 4\")\n  shot /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work/_research/spike/nodepw/kit/check/built.png  (125 colours)\n  report /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work/_research/spike/nodepw/kit/check/report.json","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b0c7f2-b636-4810-bb2b-a989930a5e0b","uuid":"c4f0a237-a069-4dba-960e-36c92c326571","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:44:38.609Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"175-     * tools. Default: on with the debug panel (dev, ?debug=1), off in a shipped game, whose players\n176-     * have the same options in the settings. `true` / `false`: always on / off; an object rebinds\n177-     * or disables (null) single actions, and they still come with the debug panel.\n178-     */\n179-    debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption;\n180-    /**\n181-     * The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate,\n182-     * sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true:\n183-     * 'top-right'; on 