{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjByK99CJ4PYLbY5yn38","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plan passes the name and line-length checks, but I found four builder traps: a bare static server would break the module imports, the Toon materials are opaque so the jar fluid won't show, the kit zip has a nested top folder, and this WebKit has no WebGPU, so only the failure message can be tested on it.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6150,"cache_read_input_tokens":424187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6150},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b0c7f2-b636-4810-bb2b-a989930a5e0b","uuid":"ae9a9dde-bf44-4bb9-8615-887cf486fb00","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:59:20.856Z","request_id":"req_011CgjByJq2tA5HvBTmCPExQ","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":2,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjByK99CJ4PYLbY5yn38","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UHo3ugjZjzh4gpvZ5gpBaf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef rep(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, (s.count(a), a[:70])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n\nrep(\"\"\"Serve it with an in-process `node:http` server on `127.0.0.1` and port 0 (or `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, reading the port from its first output line, and stopping it by its PID).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Serve it with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` ✔, reading the port from its first output line and stopping it by its PID. An in-process `node:http` server on `127.0.0.1` and port 0 also works, but it must send `Content-Type: text/javascript` for `.js`, or the harness's module imports fail.\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"Copy the whole kit into the dev folder, so `pixel-engine.js`, `check.mjs` and the guides sit at its root. **Never edit `pixel-engine.js`**; a test compares its hash with the unzipped kit's.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Download the kit (the URL is in your brief) and copy the contents of the zip's top-level `pixel-engine/` folder into the dev folder, so `pixel-engine.js`, `check.mjs` and the guides sit at its root. **Never edit `pixel-engine.js`**: record its sha256 in `vendor/pixel-engine.sha256` when you unzip, and a test compares it.\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"Sweat Jar ✔ (`lathe` for the glass; a separate scaled cylinder of `sky` fluid inside; plinth; lid; label),\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Sweat Jar ✔ (`{ lathe: [[.85,0],[.95,.1],[.95,2.1],[.75,2.4],[.75,2.55]], at: [0,.3,0], seg: 12 }` for the glass, plus plinth, lid and label; **toon materials are opaque, so fake the fluid**: a `sky` cylinder 1 cm wider than the wall, scaled in y with Drips, with a white highlight stripe),\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"19. No layout overflow at 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 640×360: widgets record their rects, and the test asserts all fit.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"19. No layout overflow at 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 640×360: widgets record their rects, and the test asserts all fit.\n20. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox have no WebGPU on this machine ✔ per its notes, so they can only test failure: a friendly \"needs a WebGPU browser\" message, no crash. Test the touch-only screen itself in Chromium's phone profile, as in test 16.\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"20. The four harness runs from section 17, all `pass`.\n21. Outside a session: normal boot with `AIHub.active` false.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"21. The four harness runs from section 17, all `pass`. Each harness frame is a separate copy of the game, which covers the brief's \"no second player\" note.\n22. Outside a session: normal boot with `AIHub.active` false.\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"| Performance unlimited, no optimisation | §13 |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| Performance unlimited, no optimisation | §13 |\n| Effort is yours to spend; an order and a cut list if you need them | §19 |\n| Machine notes: stand-ins for controller, touch, sound, second player, iPhone, TV | §17, §18 |\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 1,12p PLAN.md | cut -c1-200","description":"Patch the plan with the builder traps found in review"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6150,"cache_read_input_tokens":424187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6150},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b0c7f2-b636-4810-bb2b-a989930a5e0b","uuid":"41e401ef-ead0-4e02-a6fe-c02d31192453","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:59:29.220Z","request_id":"req_011CgjByJq2tA5HvBTmCPExQ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UHo3ugjZjzh4gpvZ5gpBaf":{"command":"cd /home/micha/d