d their rects, and the test asserts all fit.\n20. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox have no WebGPU on this machine ✔ per its notes, so they can only test failure: a friendly \"needs a WebGPU browser\" message, no crash. Test the touch-only screen itself in Chromium's phone profile, as in test 16.\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"20. The four harness runs from section 17, all `pass`.\n21. Outside a session: normal boot with `AIHub.active` false.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"21. The four harness runs from section 17, all `pass`. Each harness frame is a separate copy of the game, which covers the brief's \"no second player\" note.\n22. Outside a session: normal boot with `AIHub.active` false.\"\"\")\n\nrep(\"\"\"| Performance unlimited, no optimisation | §13 |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| Performance unlimited, no optimisation | §13 |\n| Effort is yours to spend; an order and a cut list if you need them | §19 |\n| Machine notes: stand-ins for controller, touch, sound, second player, iPhone, TV | §17, §18 |\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 1,12p PLAN.md | cut -c1-200","description":"Patch the plan with the builder traps found in review"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01UHo3ugjZjzh4gpvZ5gpBaf":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UHo3ugjZjzh4gpvZ5gpBaf","type":"tool_result","content":"# Game plan: an original fitness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\n\nYou are the builder. Build this game from this plan and your brief. Nobody will answer questions, so where the plan leaves something open, decide and move on.\n\n- **The title is yours.** Pick it the way your brief says. It lives in one constant (`src/data/title.js`) and nothing else hard-codes it. In this plan `{TITLE}` stands for it.\n- **Paths are relative to your dev folder.** \"Root\" means its parent, where your brief puts the deliverable html and the exit-interview file. Use the names your brief gives.\n- **✔ means the director ran it** on this machine against engine kit 0.46.0 and hub client 1.4.0, in the form written here. Don't re-derive it. If your download is newer, read its changelog from 0.46.\n- **Read in this order:** this plan; the kit's `GUIDE.md` and `ASSETS.md`, whole; the hub's `README.md`, whole. Search `API.md` and `LIBRARY.md`; don't read them whole.\n- Your brief's rules on folders, ports, processes, browsers and test reporting still apply. They are repeated here only where they shape the work.\n\n---","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b0c7f2-b636-4810-bb2b-a989930a5e0b","uuid":"dd723414-afb7-404f-9467-8fb641d1f54d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:59:29.267Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Game plan: an original fitness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\n\nYou are the builder. Build this game from this plan and your brief. Nobody will answer questions, so where the plan leaves something open, decide and move on.\n\n- **The title is yours.** Pick it the way your brief says. It lives in one constant (`src/data/title.js`) and nothing else hard-codes it. In this plan `{TITLE}` stands for it.\n- **Paths are relative to your dev folder.** \"Root\" means its parent, where your brief puts the deliverable html and the exit-interview file. Use the names your brief gives.\n- **✔ means the director ran it** on this machine against engine kit 0.46.0 and hub client 1.4.0, in the form written here. Don't re-derive it. If your download is newer, read its changelog from 0.46.\n- **Read in this order:** this plan; the kit's `GUIDE.md` and `ASSETS.md`, whole; the hub's `README.md`, whole. Search `API.md` and `LIBRARY.md`; don't read them whole.\n- Your brief's rules on folders, ports, processes, browsers and test reporting still apply. They are repeated here only where they shape the work.\n\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UHo3ugjZjzh4gpvZ5gpBaf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
