{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjC3mo8RncFuRiHRVqhE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MhfCBFZmYHxM6gpjpv52Wh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef rep(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, (s.count(a), a[:70])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nrep(\"\"\"20. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox have no WebGPU on this machine ✔ per its notes, so they can only test failure: a friendly \"needs a WebGPU browser\" message, no crash. Test the touch-only screen itself in Chromium's phone profile, as in test 16.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"20. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox have no `navigator.gpu` on this machine ✔, so they can only test failure: the engine's \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable\" message shows ✔ and no page error is thrown. Test the touch-only screen itself in Chromium's phone profile, as in test 16.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"If `Engine.start` rejects: show a friendly \"needs a WebGPU browser\" message, and `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"\" PLAN.md | sed -n 13,110p | cut -c1-230","description":"Patch the WebGPU failure handling and proofread the plan's first part"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1781,"cache_read_input_tokens":435754,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1781},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b0c7f2-b636-4810-bb2b-a989930a5e0b","uuid":"3ab29d02-398f-4dbc-b0b4-51e571a3b55c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:59:52.328Z","request_id":"req_011CgjC3mXVjn5uN2u1gtJNi","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MhfCBFZmYHxM6gpjpv52Wh":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211859__xc93ff1/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef rep(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, (s.count(a), a[:70])\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nrep(\"\"\"20. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox have no WebGPU on this machine ✔ per its notes, so they can only test failure: a friendly \"needs a WebGPU browser\" message, no crash. Test the touch-only screen itself in Chromium's phone profile, as in test 16.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"20. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox have no `navigator.gpu` on this machine ✔, so they can only test failure: the engine's \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable\" message shows ✔ and no page error is thrown. Test the touch-only screen itself in Chromium's phone profile, as in test 16.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"If `Engine.start` rejects: show a friendly \"needs a WebGPU browser\" message, and `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"\" PLAN.md | sed -n 13,110p | cut -c1-230","description":"Patch the WebGPU failure handling and proofread the plan's first part"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MhfCBFZmYHxM6gpjpv52Wh","type":"tool_result","content":"13:## 1. The game\n14:\n15:**A week at a spotless wellness island run by a small, polite, deeply judgmental bathroom scale. Your whole body is one dot. Keep it in the circle.**\n16:\n17:- **Genre:** fitness and balance minigame collection, inside a light life-sim week. (Catalogue genre: Sports.)\n18:- **Perspective:** isometric on the island; fixed front-on for class activities; other fixed views per activity (section 5).\n19:- **Length:** a story week of 7 short days, 16 minutes at the quickest and about an hour for a player who tries everything. Everything is also playable at once from Drop-In Class.\n20:\n21:### Pillars (use these to settle any open question)\n22:\n23:1. **You are a dot.** Almost everything is one verb: lean. The left stick, WASD or the mouse moves your centre of balance, and it has weight and sway. Poses, reps, hoops, slacklines and the finale are all different ways of movi\n24:2. **Politely judged.** Everything you do gets a calm, clinical, faintly wounding remark. You cannot lose. You can only be noted.\n25:3. **One small day at a time.** Short sessions, a morning number, a chart, a jar slowly filling.\n26:4. **Always in class.** Other people are always beside you: classmates alone, family on the couch, friends as ghosts online. Everyone wobbles.\n27:\n28:### What it takes from the source, and how it stays original\n29:\n30:| Distinctive in the source | Here |\n31:|---|---|\n32:| Your body is the controller; a centre-of-balance dot | The Dot: real sway physics on a stick, keys or mouse |\n33:| A talking device that politely judges you | Ounce, a mint retro dial scale whose dial is its face |\n34:| A calm instructor demonstrating | Coach Plumb, 81, unblinking, never off vertical |\n35:| Daily check-in, one number that sums you up, a graph | Weigh-In, Wobble Age, a line chart with a twist |\n36:| Yoga, strength, aerobics, balance games | Four stations on the island |\n37:| Minutes banked toward unlocks | Drips in the Sweat Jar |\n38:| A bright, clean, soft-spoken world | White tile plaza on a pastel island made of giant gym equipment |\n39:| A household sharing one device | Family Hour on one TV, AI Hub sessions online |\n40:\n41:**Do not use** any Nintendo name, character, look, music, level or minigame name: no Wii, Mii, Balance Board, Wii Fit Trainer, Wuhu Island or Fit Age. No white-board host, no sound-alike tunes, no channel-style menus. Mechanics\n42:\n43:**Taste rule:** no jokes about a real person's weight, body shape or eating, and no health claims. Ounce judges wobble, knees, posture and life choices, never bodies. The game asks for no real health data. The About screen says\n44:\n45:---\n46:\n47:## 2. World and cast\n48:\n49:**Tare Island** (\"Everything here starts at zero.\") is a tiny resort whose landscape is exercise equipment at enormous scale: Kettlebell Volcano (dormant, mostly), Foam Roller Hills, the Dumbbell Bridge, medicine-ball boulders.\n50:\n51:| Who | What | Voice |\n52:|---|---|---|\n53:| **Ounce** | The host, a scale. Hops after you on the island. Eyes and a red needle on a round dial: the needle is its eyebrow, and it whips, droops or spins with mood. | High, clipped, polite. \"I'd like to weigh in on that.\" \n54:| **Coach Plumb** | 81, silver bun, cyan tracksuit, a plumb bob hanging from one wrist. Demonstrates everything without effort. | Low, slow, deadpan. |\n55:| **Marguerite** | 74, classmate. Has had everything replaced and tops every leaderboard. Friendly menace. | Warm, unhurried. |\n56:| **Dennis** | 47, classmate. Here after \"an incident with a deck chair\". Overconfident, always nearly injured. Beatable by Day 3. | Quick, hearty. |\n57:| **June** | 12, Marguerite's granddaughter. Excellent and bored. | Flat. |\n58:| **Kevin** | A seagull. Lands on people. Ounce speaks of him as staff. | Squawks. |\n59:\n60:**The story in one breath:** you arrive by ferry; Ounce weighs you and gives you an alarming Wobble Age. Through the week the classmates hint that something is off (\"Has anyone ever checked that scale?\"; Coach hangs her plumb l\n61:\n62:---\n63:\n64:## 3. Structure of play\n65:\n66:### Menu map\n67:\n68:```\n69:Title (\"Press any button. Gently.\")      idle 10 s on title or any menu -> Attract\n70:└ Main Menu\n71:  ├ The Week        pick one of 3 guest slots -> Continue day N / start a week -> Island\n72:  ├ Drop-In Class   any activity at once, all open, records only, no Drips or story\n73:  ├ Family Hour     1-4 players on this screen -> Join -> The Medley -> Podium\n74:  ├ Settings\n75:  └ About & Credits\n76:```\n77:\n78:In an AI Hub session none of this appears: the game opens on its own card, then the Medley (section 12).\n79:\n80:### A day in The Week\n81:\n82:1. **Morning Weigh-In** (about 45 s, section 6): balance test, one absurd question, today's Wobble Age.\n83:2. **Free time on the island:** walk between stations, do what you like. Coach's prescription (a daily goal) pays a bonus. Ounce follows and comments.\n84:3. **Hammock** ends the day once you've done at least one activity. Leaving early earns a guilt-trip, never a block.\n85:4. **Evening Report** (about 20 s): minutes, Drips, stars, the chart, tomorrow's \"concern\", new unlocks. The light goes to dusk (`applySky(engine, skyAt(19))`), then fade to morning.\n86:\n87:### The week\n88:\n89:| Day | Test | Coach's prescription (+5 Drips) | Opens today | Story beat |\n90:|---|---|---|---|---|\n91:| 1 | Stillness | Holding Still and one other | Apologetic Tree, Startled Heron, Squats of Regret, Hoop Economics | Ferry. \"Please step on me.\" \"Ow.\" \"This dot is you. Keep it in the circle. That's it. That's the game. Everythi\n92:| 2 | Lean | 2★ in anything | Coconut Header, Apology Lunges, Reluctant Warrior (adds breathing), Locker Room | Dennis explains the deck chair. Nobody asked. |\n93:| 3 | Chase | Something you haven't done | Step Class, Slackline, The Chair Nobody Asked For | Marguerite: \"Has anyone ever checked that scale?\" Ounce: \"I'd like to weigh in on that. No.\" |\n94:| 4 | Stillness | 3 activities | Vitamin Tray, Overhead Mortgage, Tax Season | Coach hangs her plumb line by Ounce. \"You are leaning.\" \"The island is leaning.\" |\n95:| 5 | Lean | Beat Dennis at anything | Island Jog, Pier Jump, Plank Negotiation | Kevin sits on Ounce. The dial reads 7. Nobody says anything. |\n96:| 6 | Chase | 3★ anywhere | Hard versions of everything | Ounce rehearses a speech, badly, behind the Sweat Jar. |\n97:| 7 | Stillness | Stand. | The Long Stand, then the ending | The confession. The chart slides. Credits. |\n98:\n99:### Progress\n100:\n101:- **Stars:** every activity gives 0-3★ from thresholds in its data.\n102:- **Drips:** `2 + 3 × stars + floor(playSeconds / 30)`, plus the +5 goal bonus. They fill the **Sweat Jar**.\n103:- **Jar milestones** at 10, 25, 45, 70, 100, 135 and 175 Drips each unlock a Locker Room item (second headband, towel cape, \"Confidence: no visible effect\", and so on) and a remark.\n104:- **Records:** per activity, compared with data-table scores for Dennis (low), June (mid-high) and Marguerite (high). A classmate you beat reacts in the Report.\n105:- **Saves:** `localStorage`, versioned JSON, one key, 3 guest slots, written after every activity and day. Handle missing storage (Node, private mode) with an in-memory fallback.\n106:\n107:---\n108:\n109:## 4. The core: the Dot\n110:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b0c7f2-b636-4810-bb2b-a989930a5e0b","uuid":"a39ab00a-98eb-44b6-bb4f-d8571bb07fb2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:59:52.385Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"13:## 1. The game\n14:\n15:**A week at a spotless wellness island run by a small, polite, deeply judgmental bathroom scale. Your whole body is one dot. Keep it in the circle.**\n16:\n17:- **Genre:** fitness and balance minigame collection, inside a light life-sim week. (C